-- title:
--   Primes below a supersingular point come from the Drinfeld chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell \ge 3$ with $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, let $\xi \in L$ be a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota \xi = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((t))$ which, by `hK`, equals [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q * ℓ) ^ 2 * M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q * ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79): that is, $K$ is the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_H$ of level $N_0 = (q\ell)^2M'$, where $H =$ `levelH (q * ℓ) M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring with algebraically closed residue field, together with an algebra structure over which $L$ is its fraction field, such that $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ and $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$ in $L$; let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion (`hj`) the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $= t^{-1}\cdot$`jNumQ`, the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant. Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak{m}_A$, and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = qu$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   Write $C =$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` for the $j$-finite chart algebra, i.e. the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and $\mathfrak{X} =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the two-chart integral model, the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j^{-1}$-finite chart algebra along the middle chart, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and with `ιFin` the canonical morphism $\operatorname{Spec} C \to \mathfrak{X}$. Let $y \subset C$ be a maximal ideal containing the image of $\varpi$ and supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j_0 \in \Omega$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$. Let $z \in \mathfrak{X}$ and let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section of $\mathfrak{X}$ obtained from $\varpi$ through `toBase` (hypothesis `hϖz`), and assume $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$, so that $z$ lies in the special fibre. Let $y'$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin` sending $y'$ to $z$, satisfying the same supersingularity condition `hss'` for the prime $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, and with $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$ (`hy'y`).
--
--   Let $W_1$ be a complete discrete valuation ring which is a domain, $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ a ring homomorphism with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, and $f_1, u_1, v_1 \in W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W₁`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18) $= X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$. Put
--   $$S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]\big/\big(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v_1 - f_1u_1\big),$$
--   with quotient map $\mathrm{mk}$, and let $e_1$ be a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$ at its maximal ideal onto $S$. Write $\mathrm{toC}$ for the completion map $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z} \to \widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$ and $\mathrm{germY} : C \to \mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$ for the germ homomorphism at $z$ obtained from the open immersion `ιFin` (the composite of the inverses of the $\Gamma$–$\operatorname{Spec}$ adjunction isomorphism and of `ιFin.appIso ⊤` with the germ at $z$ on the image of the $j$-finite chart).
--
--   The hypothesis `hW₁` is a conjunction of seven clauses, attached to this data. (i) Constants: for every $a \in A$, $e_1$ of the completed germ at $z$ of the global section coming from $a$ equals $\mathrm{mk}(C(\sigma_1 a))$. (ii) Stability: for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q * ℓ) ξ (q * ℓ) ((q * ℓ) ^ 2 * M') (levelH (q * ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — that is, $\tau$ realises, on every quotient of integral $q$-expansions of weight-$k$ modular forms for $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ lying in $K$, the substitution by the matrix attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ as in `conjElemN (q * ℓ)`, read through any complex embedding normalised by $\iota\xi = \exp(2\pi i /(q\ell))$ — the automorphism $\tau$ maps $C$ into $C$. (iii) Congruence: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma(\ell)$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$. (iv) Linear part: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ and congruent to the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W_1$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W_1)$ such that $\theta$ is compatible with $\tau$ under $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$, $\theta$ fixes the images of the constants $C(w)$, $\theta(\mathrm{mk}\,X_{j}) \equiv \mathrm{mk}\big(\sum_i C(M_{ij})X_i\big)$ modulo $(\mathrm{mk}\,X_0,\mathrm{mk}\,X_1)^2$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$, $c \equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$, and $c \not\equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity. (v) Branch separation: for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and prime ideals $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each containing neither $\mathrm{mk}\,X_0$ nor $\mathrm{mk}\,X_1$ in the sense that at least one of the two is outside it, each containing $\mathrm{mk}(C(\sigma_1\varpi))$, and each containing an element $\mathrm{mk}(C(a_i)X_0 + C(b_i)X_1 + h)$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC}$ are different. (vi) Coefficient criterion: for every prime $P$ of $S$ not containing both $\mathrm{mk}\,X_0$ and $\mathrm{mk}\,X_1$, containing $\mathrm{mk}(C(\sigma_1\varpi))$ and containing an element $\mathrm{mk}(C(1)X_0 + C(0)X_1 + h)$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, and every $a \in C$: the element $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a)$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e_1$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$. (vii) Anchor: the Laurent series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q * ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant over $L$ with all exponents multiplied by $q\ell$) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with the difference of this element and the image of $a_0$ in $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that for all $a,b \in W_1$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_{W_1}$ the element $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0}\mathrm{coeff}_{X_0^iX_1^{e_0-i}}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit, and such that $e_1$ of the completed germ of that difference equals $\mathrm{mk}(h)$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses, let $\mathfrak{p}$ be a prime ideal of $C$ containing the image of $\varpi$, with $\mathfrak{p} \le y$ and $\mathfrak{p} \ne y$. Then there exists a prime ideal $P$ of $S$ such that: $P$ is prime; at least one of $\mathrm{mk}\,X_0$, $\mathrm{mk}\,X_1$ lies outside $P$; $\mathrm{mk}(C(\sigma_1\varpi)) \in P$; and for every $a \in C$ one has $a \in \mathfrak{p}$ if and only if $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a)$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e_1$, i.e. $e_1(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a)) \in P$. Thus $\mathfrak{p}$ is the contraction of $P$ under the completed germ map at the supersingular point.
--
--   This identifies every prime of the $j$-finite chart algebra strictly below a supersingular closed point in the special fibre — in particular every irreducible component of the special fibre through that point — as the contraction of a prime of the Drinfeld local model $S$ that contains the uniformiser but not the whole maximal ideal, hence of one of its branch primes. It is the passage from the global chart to the Katz–Mazur style local chart at a supersingular point, and is used by the statements that count the components through such a point, that transport them by the level automorphisms, and that compare components via the blow-up chart.
